  "id": "humoral-theory",
  "term": "humoral theory",
  "definition": "Humoral theory is a traditional view that links human health, including mental health, to basic natural elements—Fire, Water, Earth, and Air. In the source context, it is used as a framework for thinking about how environmental factors and nature-based experiences may influence wellbeing.",
